From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:33:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/42] cuda: carry the Q8_1 cache entry of the layer input
 into the routed-MoE split

Decode/verify layers run as three graph computes per device; the scheduler
splits before the first routed MUL_MAT_ID (expert-cache staging, #129) and
graph_compute clears the Q8_1 cache, so the routed MoE re-quantized the
layer input the hc mixer had just published (48 quantize_q8_1 per pass).

The previous compute now hands on its exact entries (written like
quantize_q8_1: only the Q8_0 hc epilogue marks them); a compute whose first
node is a routed MUL_MAT_ID takes the entry for that node's activation.
Captured graphs record the entries their capture produced (replays hand
them on) and are recaptured when the carried entry differs from the one
they were captured with (q8_carry_sig). GGML_CUDA_Q8_1_CARRY=0: off;
GGML_CUDA_Q8_1_CARRY_LOG=1: report carries; GGML_CUDA_GRAPH_TRACE also
counts carry-only recaptures. Bit-identical (FINDINGS 1011).

(cherry picked from commit c2ab621c8a6ffa7b6b167222be68a4ab350b1bd0)
